1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:11,870
Slide 21 outlines OPERATIONAL DESKTOP SAFETY GUARDRAILS. Sarah, James, what guardrails must we enforce on every desktop agent?

2
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:14,797
Guardrail 1: RAM Ceiling Governor.

3
00:00:14,797 --> 00:00:21,263
We bind the desktop agent inside a Windows Job Object with a hard 200MB memory ceiling.

4
00:00:21,263 --> 00:00:27,730
If a subprocess starts leaking memory, the OS kills and restarts it in 50 milliseconds!

5
00:00:28,130 --> 00:00:30,435
Guardrail 2: Clipboard Purge Hook!

6
00:00:30,435 --> 00:00:33,621
Never let an agent hold clipboard data forever!

7
00:00:33,621 --> 00:00:41,350
After 30 seconds, the agent wipes its memory buffer so your copied passwords and credit cards don't linger in RAM!

8
00:00:41,750 --> 00:00:44,316
And Guardrail 3: Power-Aware Throttle!

9
00:00:44,316 --> 00:00:53,770
The instant your laptop unplugged from the wall, the agent throttles heavy OCR screen scraping to preserve 100% of your battery for flights!

10
00:00:54,170 --> 00:01:01,180
Strict operational guardrails ensure your desktop agent remains a servant, not a resource-hogging tyrant.

